    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Senior-Lecturer-in-Engineering_JR105172": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Engineering is an academic discipline within the School of Engineering and Energy. The Engineering team teach key and emerging areas of Engineering at the undergraduate and postgraduate levels. We specialize in Environmental Engineering, Electrical and Renewable Energy Engineering and industrial Control & Automation Engineering. Industrial Control & Automation Engineering at Murdoch highlights a strong practical, industry-relevant learning approach, built around authentic, workshop-based activities that develop hands-on technical and professional skills. The area includes a focus on control theory and control systems, including PLC and SCADA systems, aligned with real-world design, commissioning, and implementation needs in local industry sectors. More broadly, Murdoch Engineering is nationally recognised and has a strong track record of student outcomes, including high rankings in QILT for overall quality of educational experience in Engineering. Engineering is taught at the Murdoch campus and offshore. Your New Role!   We are seeking a Lecturer (Level B) or Senior Lecturer (Level C) to join our Industrial Control and Automation Engineering discipline within the School of Engineering and Energy. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to a nationally recognised Engineering program through high-quality teaching, impactful research and industry engagement. You will teach across undergraduate and postgraduate programs, contribute to curriculum innovation and help prepare graduates for careers in rapidly evolving engineering industries. The successful candidate will have expertise in Industrial Control & Automation Engineering or a related field, with experience in areas such as control systems, industrial automation, instrumentation, PLCs, SCADA systems, robotics, mechatronics or intelligent automation. Based at our South Street campus, this position also includes teaching at one of Murdoch University's partner institutions in China. The successful candidate will be willing and able to undertake two international teaching visits each year, typically totalling four to six months annually. Your Key responsibilities will include – Deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate Engineering programs. Contribute to curriculum development and continuous improvement of courses and units. Conduct impactful research and contribute to scholarly publications. Engage with industry and professional stakeholders to enhance teaching and research outcomes. Supervise honours and postgraduate students, as appropriate to level. Contribute to School, College and University service activities. Teach at Murdoch University's partner institution in China. Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details.   Level B Level C   What We Offer You! This Continuous, Full Time attracts a remuneration of:   Lecturer Level B : $115,512 - $136,831 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.   Senior Lecturer Level C $141,088 - $162,403 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: A PhD in Industrial Control & Automation Engineering or a closely related discipline. Expertise in one or more areas including industrial automation, control systems, PLCs, SCADA systems, instrumentation, robotics, mechatronics or intelligent automation. Demonstrated teaching experience at undergraduate and/or postgraduate level. Strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to work collaboratively. Commitment to high-quality teaching, research and student outcomes. Ability and willingness to undertake international teaching visits in China. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Visa sponsorship and relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to David Parlevliet , Dean of Engineering and Energy, and quote JR105172 as the reference. Applications Close on 26th October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Centre-Director--Australian-National-Phenome-Centre--ANPC-_JR105851": {
      "title": "Centre Director, Australian National Phenome Centre (ANPC)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Australian National Phenome Centre (ANPC) is a national Core Facility for high-resolution metabolic phenotyping and translational bioscience. Based within the Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research in Perth’s Murdoch Health Precinct, the Centre integrates advanced Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR), mass spectrometry, automation and bioinformatics platforms to support industrial-scale biological analysis and population-scale phenotyping at the interface of research, healthcare and industry. The ANPC is a key platform within Murdoch University’s Health Futures Institute. The Centre supports research across a broad range of disciplines, including precision medicine and human health, population health and epidemiology, chronic disease prevention, nutrition and metabolic health, agriculture and food systems, environmental science, and systems biology research. For more information about the Australian National Phenome Centre (ANPC) please refer to the ANPC brochure . Your New Role!   Reporting to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Research and Innovation, the Centre Director provides strategic, scientific and operational leadership for the Australian National Phenome Centre (ANPC). The role is responsible for setting the Centre’s vision and direction, maximising the impact of its infrastructure, and positioning the Centre as globally recognised leader in precision health, translational bioscience and population-scale discovery. You will lead a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technical specialists, drive intentionally competitive research programs, secure major research investment, and support the translation of research outcomes into clinical, public health, commercial and societal impact. Murdoch University welcomes expressions of interest from Associate Professors, recently appointment Professors and equivalent research leaders seeking to broaden their impact through the leadership of a nationally significant research capability. Your key responsibilities will include – Provide strategic, scientific and operational leadership for ANPC, setting the Centre’s vision and direction and maximising the impact of its research infrastructure Drive internationally competitive research programs and secure major research investment to advance prevision health, phenomics and translational research Build strategic partnership across academia, healthcare, government, and industry to support research translation and impact Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement and the ANPC Brochure for further details.   What We Offer You! This, Fixed Term (5 Years) | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts the following remuneration: $217,824.00 (pro rata) at the Academic Level E plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, potential market loading will be considered for the right candidate undefined $169,509.00 to 186,557.00 (pro rata) at the Academic Level D plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, potential market loading will be considered for the right candidate    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: ·         Flexible work arrangements ·         Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role ·         Indigenous Language Allowance ·         Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit ·         Employee Assistance Program ·         On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria and qualification requirement(s) (Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement) Your most recent resume (CV)   What you’ll bring to the role: A doctoral qualification (PhD or equivalent) in a relevant discipline such as biomedical science, health and medical research, metabolomics, systems biology, population health, bioinformatics, precision health or a closely related field. Internationally recognised expertise in precision health, metabolomics, phenomics, systems biology or a related biomedical discipline Demonstrated success in leading large-scale translational, clinical, cohort, epidemiology or multidisciplinary research programs A strong track record in securing competitive research funding and developing internationally competitive research programs Proven ability to translate research outcomes into clinical, public health, policy, industry, innovation or commercial applications with evidence of national and/or international research impact Ability to undertake domestic and international travel and work across Murdoch University campuses, the Australia National Phenome Centre (ANPC), partner organisations and clinical and research precincts as required Ability to work within laboratory, clinical, cohort and research environments to support research programs and strategic initiative Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure.   Applicants should refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Peter Eastwood, Deputy Vice Chancellor, Research and Innovation, Peter.Eastwood@murdoch.edu.au , and quote JR105851 as the reference.   Applications Close on 05 November 2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Senior-Research-Fellow-or-Principal-Research-Fellow_JR105738": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow or Principal Research Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Food Futures Institute is one of Murdoch University’s research institutes, focused on developing innovating solutions for sustainable food, forestry, and fibre production. This position is based within the Centre for Crop and Food Innovation (CCFI) and the State Agricultural Biotechnology Centre (SABC). CCFI conducts research in broadacre and horticultural crops, bringing together academic and research staff who work with industry partners to improve crop yield, quality and resilience. The Centre also supports more than 50 Higher Degree by Research students and is ideally place to capitalise on new technologies and investments in crop agriculture. SABC is Western Australia’s collaborative university-based centre for agricultural and veterinary biotechnology, providing access to specialised technologies, equipment and research facilities that support collaboration across agricultural, environmental and conversation, molecular, biomedical and veterinary sciences.   Your New Role!   We are seeking to appoint either a Senior Research Fellow (Level C) or a Principal Research Fellow (Level D) in Murdoch University, South Street Campus. As a Senior Research Fellow (Level C) , you are expected to lead and coordinate innovative genomics and pre- breeding research to advance genetic gain in pulse crops. The role involves delivering multidisciplinary research programs, including field trials, genotyping and sequencing, genomic and bioinformatics analyses, and AI-enabled breeding approaches. You will contribute to genomic resource development, public research outcomes, secure competitive funding, supervise HDR students and research staff, and collaborate with national and international research partners. Working closely with the Director of CCFI/SABC, you will provide scientific leadership in the successful delivery of GRDC-funded project, Achieving Improved Genetic Gain for Yield in Chickpea, Faba Bean and Lentil Using Genetic Diversity, while contributing to Murdoch University’s strategic research priorities in Food and Agriculture. As a Principal Research Fellow (Level D), you will provide strategic leadership in genomics, functional genomics, pre- breeding and AI-enabled crop improvement across wheat, pulse and horticultural crop research programs. This role involves developing and leading internationally recognised research programs integrating genomics, phenomics, bioinformatics and artificial intelligence, establishing multi-disciplinary research initiatives, fostering strategic partnerships, securing major research funding, supervising and mentoring researchers, and driving the strategic growth and international reputation of CCFI, SABC and Murdoch University. Your key responsibilities will include – Senior Research Fellow (Level C) Provide strategic leadership in developing and delivering innovative research programs aligned with CCFI priorities, enhancing national and international research impact Lead internationally competitive research in genomics, functional genomics, molecular breeding, AI-enabled crop improvement, and related disciplines Build and maintain strategic collaborations with universities, government, industry, and international partners to advance multidisciplinary and translational research outcomes Secure competitive research funding, leading major grant applications, and oversee high-quality research programs including glasshouse, controlled-environment, and field-based experiments Apply advanced genomics, sequencing bioinformatics, molecular genetics, and AI methodologies to deliver impactful crop improvement and agricultural biotechnology outcomes, translating research into practical applications Publish high-quality scholarly outputs, supervise and mentor HDR students and research staff, contribute to teaching and postgraduate education, and provide leadership in governance, strategic planning, and professional service activities Principal Research Fellow (Level D) Drive and shape internationally recognised research programs in plant genomics, molecular breeding, artificial intelligence, and crop improvement across diverse agricultural systems Lead multidisciplinary research teams and deliver innovative solutions to challenges in crop improvement, sustainable agriculture, and food security, aligned with the University and national research priorities Design and oversee complex laboratory, glasshouse, controlled-environment and field-related research programs, applying advanced genomics, sequencing, bioinformatics, quantitative genetics, and AI enabled approaches Secure major national and international research funding, develop industry partnership and build strategic collaborations with universities, government agencies, industry, CGIAR centres, and global research organisations Translate research discoveries into practical breeding and agricultural applications, promoting industry adoption, commercialisation, and stakeholder engagement Produce high-impact research outputs, contribute to the strategic growth and reputation of CCFI and SABC, and provide academic leadership, mentorship, governance, and professional service within the University and broader research community   Please refer to the Position Descriptions for further details. ·       Senior Research Fellow (Level C) ·       Principal Research Fellow (Level D)   What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (3 years) |Full Time (37.5 hours per week) position attracts a remuneration of the following Level C $141,088- $162,403 (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions Level D $169,509 - $186,557 (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions   You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   ·       Flexible work arrangements ·       Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role ·       Indigenous Language Allowance ·       Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit ·       Employee Assistance Program ·       On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - ·       A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria and qualification requirement(s) (Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement) Your most recent resume (CV)     What you’ll bring to the role: Senior Research Fellow (Level C) PhD in Agricultural Biotechnology, Genetics, Plant Breeding or any other relevant subject with at least five years’ research experience in crop genomics and pre-breeding, and an established national and emerging international research reputation Demonstrated ability to develop, lead and manage independent research programs in genomics, functional genomics, molecular breeding, crop improvement or related fields, supported by a strong publication record Proven success in securing research outcomes through multidisciplinary projects, collaboration with industry, government and international partners, and translating research into impact Demonstrated experience supervising and mentoring HDR students, postdoctoral researchers and research staff, with strong leadership, organisational and project management skills Excellent communication skills, including scientific publications, grant writing and presentations, together with a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and a safe, respectful workplace Principal Research Fellow (Level D) PhD in Plant Science, Plant Genetics, Plant Breeding, Genomics, Agricultural Biotechnology, or a related discipline, with an internationally recognised reputation and outstanding research impact in plant genomics, functional genomics, molecular breeding, quantitative genetics or related fields Demonstrated success leading internationally competitive research programs, securing major national and international research funding, and delivering significant scientific, industry and societal outcomes Expertise in plant genomics, functional genomics, molecular breeding, quantitative genetics, high-throughput sequencing technologies, bioinformatics, artificial intelligence, and digital technologies of crop improvement Proven ability to lead multidisciplinary and multi-institutional research teams, establish strategic collaborations, and build impactful partnership across universities, industry, government and international organisations Demonstrated academic leadership through supervision and mentoring of researchers and HDR students, strategic contributions to research capacity building and governance, and a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and research integrity   Applicants should refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Visa sponsorship and relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Rajeev Varshney, Director of the State Agricultural Biotechnology Centre and Director of the Centre for Crop and Food, rajeev.varshney@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105738 as the reference.   Applications Close on 01/11/2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
