    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Sustainable-Farm-Project-Officer_JR105740": {
      "title": "Sustainable Farm Project Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout The Team Our Sustainability team is passionate, collaborative and dedicated to driving sustainability initiatives across Murdoch University's campuses and farms. Working across Sustainability Ethos, Climate Action and Nature Positive priorities, the team delivers projects that create meaningful environmental outcomes. In this role, you'll contribute to Murdoch University's Nature Positive aspirations by supporting biodiversity, habitat restoration and sustainable land management initiatives across the University's unique farm and conservation landscapes.   Your New Role!   As the Sustainable Farm Project Officer, you will play a key role in delivering innovative farm regeneration and environmental restoration projects across Murdoch University's South Street campus. Working as part of the Office of the PVC Sustainability, you will help enhance biodiversity, expand wildlife corridors, restore wetlands and native habitats and support nature positive outcomes across the University's farms and surrounding conservation areas.   In this newly created role, you'll work closely with sustainability specialists, farm teams, researchers and academic staff to implement on-ground projects, coordinate contractors, monitor project outcomes, and contribute to major sustainability initiatives supported by significant external funding. Your work will directly support Murdoch University's environmental goals and long-term sustainability strategy.   Key Responsibilities Deliver sustainable farming, environmental restoration, and biodiversity projects in collaboration with key stakeholders. Coordinate contractors and service providers undertaking restoration works, including weed management, fencing, revegetation, and site maintenance. Support habitat restoration across farms, wetlands, woodlands, and conservation areas. Monitor project outcomes, maintain project records, and assist with reporting against project objectives, budgets, and timelines. Source and apply best-practice advice on ecological restoration, weed management, and native vegetation establishment.     Please refer to the Position Description for further details.   What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (2 Years) | Part time (15 hours per week) attracts a starting salary of $93k (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.  The position is also eligible for salary step progression within the classification level in accordance with Murdoch University's Enterprise Agreement.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV)     What you’ll bring to the role: A Bachelor’s degree or Diploma in Sustainable Agriculture, Soil Science, Environmental Management, or a related field. Experience delivering environmental restoration projects, particularly in sensitive ecological environments. Demonstrated experience managing environmental management contractors and services. Knowledge of environmental weed control and ecological restoration practices. A current Class C Driver’s Licence. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Leah Knapp, Manager Sustainability, l.knapp@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105740 as the reference.  Applications Close on 21 October 2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Veterinary-Nurse--Surgery--1_JR105618": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse (Surgery)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The small animal surgery referral service offers specialty services in both soft tissue and oncologic surgery, and orthopaedic and neurosurgery. Our full range of facilities and state of the art surgical equipment, coupled with integrated support from specialist level care in anaesthesia, 24h intensive care, internal medicine, advanced diagnostic imaging and excellent nursing standards enable us to manage the most complex surgical challenges and ensure that our patients receive a very high standard of care across all aspects of surgical management. You would be joining a team of 7 veterinary nurses; the service is open to clientele 08:00 -18:00 Weekdays. Your New Role!   The key purpose of this role is to provide high quality veterinary nursing care to animals in The Animal Hospital At Murdoch University. Your Key responsibilities will include – Provide all aspects of veterinary nursing care as per the Certificate IV of Veterinary Nursing and the Prescribed Duties of Veterinary Nurses within the Vet Surgeons Act of WA. Comply with University and TAHMU policies, procedures and protocols. Comply with The Veterinary Surgeons’ Act of WA and other veterinary industry related Acts and Regulations. Liaise with clinical areas within the hospital to coordinate daily availability of equipment and technical support. Assist clinicians with examinations, workups, procedures, treatments and surgeries. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (12 Month) | Part time or Full Time (up to 37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $74,809K – $79,802K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, with the option to sacrifice 5% of your superannuation into your salary.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Completion of a Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing or equivalent, or completion of a relevant Veterinary Nursing Diploma level qualification registrable in Western Australia. Demonstrated confidence and skill when handling and restraining small animals. Excellent knowledge of diagnostic and surgical equipment as well as sterilising and aseptic techniques. Demonstrated experience and exposure to various surgical procedures and patient care in a general practice setting. Excellent organisational, time and workload management skills, including the ability to prioritise workload to meet strict deadlines. Highly effective communication, customer service and interpersonal skills, and the demonstrated ability to interact constructively and collaboratively with staff at all levels of the organisation. Demonstrated ability to use initiative, assume responsibility for tasks and projects and to resolve problems. Proven ability to work independently as well as fitting seamlessly into a team environment. A strong interest in developing skills within a specialised area. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Sam Watkins , Surgery Coordinator, sam.watkins@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105618 as the reference. Applications Close on 23rd October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
